35,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, the wall is single plasterboard. A phone call inside is audible from the nearest desk.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, that confirms the sound issue. I found the invoices: 68,000 yen for nine small bookings last year.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: I checked the desks. Three keyboards have crumbs, and bins go out daily. It’s messy.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: The last difficult talk happened across the open desks, in front of everyone. They went silent for two weeks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, that silence is costly. I found eleven callouts for equipment rooms, none for the empty store.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, 68,000 yen for nine bookings is a waste. We need a space that actually works for us, not just a place to hide.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, exactly. We are paying for space we cannot use properly. I also have the fit-out quotes: 141,000 for a meeting setup, 96,000 for a kitchen.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Daisuke, those quotes are huge. But I found the lunch trip takes twenty-five minutes. Most of us go three or four days a week.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, twenty-five minutes is a long walk for a simple meal. It shows how much we value that break.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the kitchen quote is cheaper, but the meeting space costs more. I need to know which one saves us the most hidden hours.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, the meeting space costs more, but the kitchen saves us the daily twenty-five minute walk. Which one do you think saves more time overall?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, the kitchen saves daily time, but the meeting space stops us paying 68,000 yen externally. I need to see which total is lower.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, the crumbs prove we already eat here. A kitchen just makes it official and stops the mess spreading to our desks.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, the mess is a symptom. The real loss is that we have no private place to speak, so we avoid difficult conversations entirely.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, the silence costs us more than the yen. I found the old fridge was cleared twice by one person. We need a space that doesn’t demand unpaid labor.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Servas, you are right. The silence is the real cost. I will support whatever option gives us that privacy.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, I agree on the privacy, but I still need the numbers to balance the books. I will support the option that stops the monthly drain.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, I agree. But if we eat here, the mess stays here. I want a kitchen so the crumbs stop landing on my keyboard.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, a kitchen solves the crumbs, but it does not solve the silence. We need a place where words can be spoken without fear of being overheard.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, the fridge clearing shows unpaid labor. A meeting space with a shared calendar distributes the burden fairly, unlike a kitchen.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
