60,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, a calendar does not stop sound. The wall is thin. We need a room where we can actually speak without being overheard.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, the wall is thin, but the invoices show we pay 68,000 yen for space we can’t use. I need to stop that drain.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Daisuke, but the kitchen quote is cheaper than the meeting one. Plus, I hate crumbs on my keyboard.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Shion, the wall is thin, but the silence is thicker. We need a place where difficult words can be spoken without fear of being overheard.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Shion, the wall is thin, but the calendar stops the unpaid labor. I support the meeting space to distribute the burden fairly.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Servas, you are right. The wall is thin, but the silence is thicker. We need a place where difficult words can be spoken without fear of being overheard.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, I hear you, but the numbers are cold. The meeting space stops the external drain. I cannot ignore the invoices.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, I agree the silence is bad, but a quiet room doesn't fix the crumbs. I still want the kitchen to keep my desk clean.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, a quiet room keeps the mess out, but it also keeps the people out. We need a place where we can actually talk, not just hide.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, a quiet room isolates us further. The meeting space forces interaction and fair scheduling, preventing the unpaid labor I saw in the fridge logs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, a calendar is just a list. It doesn't stop the sound leaking through that thin wall. We need actual privacy, not just a booking slot.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, the calendar is a tool, not a solution. I need the financial certainty. I will vote for the option that stops the 68,000 yen drain.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, a calendar doesn't stop the noise. I want the kitchen so the crumbs stay in the room, not on my keyboard.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, a calendar manages time, not trust. We need a space where we can finally speak without fear of being overheard.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shion, the wall is thin, but the calendar stops the unpaid labor. I support the meeting space to distribute the burden fairly.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, I vote for the Quiet Room. It is the only option that respects the thin wall and gives us the privacy to speak freely.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I vote for the Meeting Space. It stops the 68,000 yen drain and the quotes show it is the only viable financial path.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, I vote for the Open Kitchen. It keeps the crumbs off my keyboard and saves us the long lunch walk.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, I vote for the Quiet Room. It is the only place where the silence can finally be broken without fear.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Shion, I vote for the Meeting Space. The shared calendar ensures fair use and stops the hidden labor I found in the logs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
